samples/
notes/
CLAUDE.md

# Local TLS dev certificates (mkcert) — never commit private keys
certs/
__pycache__/
# Assembled Cloudflare origin for the paragraph-analysis satellite (build.sh output)
paragraph-analysis/public/
electron/node_modules/
electron/dist/
electron/out/
electron/vendor/
electron/src/build-flags.json

# ── AI/dev-facing working notes — NOT tracked (Seth, 2026-07-29) ──────────────
# "md files meant for AI models' use during development shouldn't be tracked, unless
# they're specifically meant for public use by others cloning the repository."
# These are working notes and task briefs; they change constantly, and one of them
# (worker/docs/approved-domains.md) once leaked the operator's whole partner list into
# a public repo. Keep them locally, out of git.
tasks/
corpus-manager/PLAN.md
worker/docs/approved-domains.md
apps/*/public/

# ── plans/ IS THE EXCEPTION, and it is tracked ON PURPOSE (Seth, 2026-08-07) ──
# "Maybe we can make a plans/ folder and exempt it, and make sure that nothing goes in
# there that's secret. If the code is open source anyway, plans for features, etc won't
# increase security risk at all. But it would be good to keep them in a specific place."
# It satisfies the "unless they're specifically meant for public use by others cloning the
# repository" clause above: design docs an adopter (SIL LSDev, Payap) would want.
# ⚠ NOT under docs/ — docs/ IS THE WEBSITE, so anything there is SERVED. plans/ is tracked
# but never published. See plans/README.md for what may and may not go in it.
!plans/

# npm deps for local test tooling (linkedom for DOM-in-node parser tests) — never served, never committed
node_modules/
